.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-journal-2026-05-20
.Nd working notes of 2026-05-20
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss jotain.service aborts with vc-git-root void
.Ss Symptom
The
.Ql "jotain"
systemd user service exited with
.Ql "status=255/EXCEPTION"
shortly after
.Ql "init.el"
finished loading:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Saving file /home/user/.config/emacs/var/custom.el...
Wrote /home/user/.config/emacs/var/custom.el
Symbol's function definition is void: vc-git-root
Wrote /home/user/.config/emacs/var/recentf-save.el
Wrote /home/user/.config/emacs/var/save-place.el
jotain.service: Main process exited, code=exited, status=255/EXCEPTION
.Ed
.Ss Root cause
.Ql "lisp/init-vc.el"
added
.Ql "jotain-git-stats--invalidate-current-buffer"
to a global
.Ql "after-save-hook" ,
and the
.Ql "jotain-git-stats"
doom-modeline segment calls
.Ql "vc-git-root"
on every redraw.
Both call sites assumed
.Ql "vc-git.el"
was loaded, but the
.Ql "use-package vc-git"
block sets only
.Ql ":ensure nil"
+
.Ql ":bind" ,
so the library autoloads on
.Ql "C-x C-g" ,
not on init.
.Pp
During first-run startup,
.Ql "use-package :ensure t"
calls
.Ql "package-install" ,
which writes
.Ql "custom-file"
via
.Ql "package--save-selected-packages" .
That fires the global
.Ql "after-save-hook" ,
the hook calls
.Ql "vc-git-root" ,
the symbol is void, and the daemon aborts before reaching
.Ql "server-start" .
.Pp
The two
.Ql "declare-function"
lines for
.Ql "vc-git-root"
in the file silenced the byte-compiler but never arranged a runtime load.
.Ql "vc-git-root"
has no
.Ql ";;;###autoload"
cookie upstream, so nothing implicitly loads it.
.Ss Fix
.Ql "lisp/init-vc.el"
— replaced both
.Ql "(vc-git-root FILE)"
calls outside the interactive
.Ql "jotain-switch-git-status-buffer"
command with
.Ql "(locate-dominating-file FILE \(dq.git\(dq)" .
.Ql "locate-dominating-file"
is in
.Ql "files.el"
(always loaded) and is what
.Ql "vc-git-root"
calls through
.Ql "vc-find-root"
internally; the only thing dropped is a
.Ql "vc-file-getprop"
cache, which is immaterial at modeline-render frequency.
.Pp
Also removed the now-unused second
.Ql "(declare-function vc-git-root …)"
above the
.Ql "with-eval-after-load 'doom-modeline"
form.
The first
.Ql "declare-function"
and the
.Ql "(require 'vc-git)"
inside
.Ql "jotain-switch-git-status-buffer"
remain, since that command keeps using
.Ql "vc-git-root"
and demands the library at call time.
.Ss Out of scope
The TLS errors against
.Ql "elpa.gnu.org"
/
.Ql "elpa.nongnu.org"
/
.Ql "stable.melpa.org"
in the same journal come from the host's corporate proxy.
Emacs recovers from them; they did not cause the abort, only ~50 s of extra startup.
Silencing the eager refresh
.No \&( Ns Ql "jotain--package-refresh-once"
in
.Ql "init.el" )
when offline is a separate, lower-priority change.
.Ss Fix devenv shell, pull Emacs 31 from emacs-overlay
.Ss Summary
Devenv shell evaluation failed with
.Ql "error: attribute 'emacs31' missing"
because the pinned nixpkgs only ships
.Ql "emacs30" .
Wired
.Ql "nix-community/emacs-overlay"
into both
.Ql "flake.nix"
and
.Ql "devenv.yaml"
and switched
.Ql "emacs.nix"
to consume
.Ql "pkgs.emacs-git"
/
.Ql "pkgs.emacs-macport"
from the overlay instead of the non-existent
.Ql "pkgs.emacs31{-macport}" .
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "flake.nix" Ns No "\fP"
— added
.Ql "emacs-overlay"
input
.No \&( Ns Ql "inputs.nixpkgs.follows = \(dqnixpkgs\(dq" )
and inserted
.Ql "emacs-overlay.overlays.default"
before
.Ql "self.overlays.default"
in
.Ql "pkgsFor" .
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "devenv.yaml" Ns No "\fP"
— added the same
.Ql "emacs-overlay"
input, pinned to the rev
.Ql "flake.lock"
resolved to so both locks agree.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "devenv.nix" Ns No "\fP"
— accepted the new
.Ql "inputs"
module arg and applied
.Ql "inputs.emacs-overlay"
before the project overlay.
Added
.Ql "nix-community"
to the
.Ql "cachix.pull"
list (that is where
.Ql "emacs-git"
binaries live).
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "emacs.nix" Ns No "\fP"
—
.Ql "basePackage"
now selects
.Ql "pkgs.emacs-git"
for every variant except
.Ql "macport" ,
which uses
.Ql "pkgs.emacs-macport" .
Standalone invocation
.No \&( Ns Ql "nix-build emacs.nix" )
re-applies the overlay through a new
.Ql "overlays = [ (import …) ]"
arg in the default
.Ql "pkgs"
derivation, pulling the rev from
.Ql "flake.lock" .
Fixed
.Ql "srcRepo"
default to include
.Ql "mainline"
so autoreconf runs (emacs-overlay's
.Ql "emacs-git"
is a git checkout).
Cache-parity comment block updated to reference
.Ql "pkgs.emacs-git"
instead of the no-longer-existing
.Ql "pkgs.emacs31" .
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "Justfile" Ns No "\fP"
— added
.Ql "emacs-overlay"
to
.Ql "shared_inputs"
so
.Ql "just update"
and
.Ql "just verify"
keep both locks in sync on that rev.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "CLAUDE.md" Ns No "\fP,"
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/architecture/overview.mdx" Ns No "\fP,"
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/architecture/nix-build.mdx" Ns No "\fP,"
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/installation.mdx" Ns No "\fP,"
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/introduction.mdx" Ns No "\fP"
— replaced stale
.Ql "pkgs.emacs30"
/
.Ql "pkgs.emacs30-macport"
references and re-targeted the cache-parity invariant onto
.Ql "pkgs.emacs-git" .
.El
.Ss Verification
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ql "nix-instantiate --eval"
proves
.Ql "(import ./emacs.nix {}).outPath == pkgs.emacs-git.outPath"
for the pinned overlay rev — the mainline build remains a binary-cache hit on
.Ql "nix-community.cachix.org" .
.It
.Ql "devenv shell -- emacs --batch --version"
reports
.Ql "GNU Emacs 32.0.50"
(the master branch has already moved past 31;
.Ql "emacs-git"
advertises itself externally as
.Ql "20260519.0" ).
.It
All seven assertions from
.Ql "devenv.nix" Ns No "'s"
.Ql "enterTest"
block pass when run manually inside the shell
.No \&( Ns Ql "emacs" ,
.Ql "emacsclient" ,
.Ql "etags"
resolve into the
.Ql "jotain-emacs-full"
store path;
.Ql "--init-directory"
loads this repo's config;
.Ql "eask"
is on PATH).
.It
.Ql "nix flake check --no-build"
evaluates clean.
.It
.Ql "just verify"
reports OK on every shared input
.No \&( Ns Ql "nixpkgs" ,
.Ql "treefmt-nix" ,
.Ql "emacs-overlay" ).
.El
.Ss Notes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The user-level
.Ql "~/.config/nix/nix.conf"
does not list
.Ql "nix-community.cachix.org"
as a substituter, so the very first
.Ql "devenv shell"
after this change still has to fetch the
.Ql "emacs-git"
binary via the explicit
.Ql "cachix.pull"
declaration (devenv layers it in).
Users without devenv can either add the substituter to
.Ql "nix.conf"
directly or pass
.Ql "--option extra-substituters https://nix-community.cachix.org --option extra-trusted-public-keys nix-community.cachix.org-1:mB9FSh9qf2dCimDSUo8Zy7bkq5CX+/rkCWyvRCYg3Fs=" .
.It
.Ql "emacs-overlay" Ns No "'s"
.Ql "emacs-git"
tracks master and is currently internally
.Ql "32.0.50" .
The repo's \(dqEmacs 31+\(dq framing still holds since
.Ql "emacs ≥ 31"
is satisfied; bumping to a tagged
.Ql "emacs-31"
would require waiting for the upstream release.
.El
